  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_common" xml:space="preserve"><value>Shared Streamline services that pass the game's rendering resources and frame data to feature plugins and manage their NVIDIA NGX connection.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_deepdvc" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to RTX Dynamic Vibrance, an AI color-enhancement effect that adjusts saturation. It is not an upscaler or frame generator.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_directsr" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to DirectSR super resolution through DirectX 12, using the upscaling variant selected by the game.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_dlss" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to DLSS Super Resolution for AI upscaling, or DLAA for anti-aliasing at native resolution. This is the Streamline plugin, not nvngx_dlss.dll.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_dlss_d" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to DLSS Ray Reconstruction, which replaces ray-tracing denoisers with AI reconstruction. This is the Streamline plugin, not nvngx_dlssd.dll.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_dlss_g" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to DLSS Frame Generation, which creates additional frames from the game's rendered frames. This is the Streamline plugin, not nvngx_dlssg.dll.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_interposer" xml:space="preserve"><value>The game's entry point into Streamline. It loads feature plugins and routes the graphics API calls Streamline needs.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_nis" xml:space="preserve"><value>NVIDIA Image Scaling: spatial upscaling and sharpening, or sharpening alone. This is a separate algorithm from DLSS.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_nvperf" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects Streamline to NVIDIA Nsight Perf SDK for GPU performance measurement and profiling. It is not an upscaler or frame generator.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_pcl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Records PC latency markers and timing measurements during gameplay. It measures latency; Reflex handles low-latency control separately.</value></data>
  <data name="Linux_StreamlineDescription_reflex" xml:space="preserve"><value>Connects the game to NVIDIA Reflex low-latency control and its frame-rate limiter. PC latency statistics are handled separately by sl.pcl.dll in newer SDKs.</value></data>
